diff --git a/docs/hugo/content/contributing/testing.md b/docs/hugo/content/contributing/testing.md
index 44662a3f1773bfd49a448408bf2b0270d90c6d2b..0492f7798772ce06e46f5352dfc966f57c3112ac 100644
--- a/docs/hugo/content/contributing/testing.md
+++ b/docs/hugo/content/contributing/testing.md
@@ -20,6 +20,10 @@ To run the test and produce a new recording you will need to have set the requir
 for an Azure Service Principal: `AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID`, `AZURE_TENANT_ID`, `AZURE_CLIENT_ID`, and `AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET`. 
 This Service Principal will need access to the subscription to create and delete resources.
 
+When running in GitHub Actions, the CI workflows no longer use `AZURE_CLIENT_ID` or `AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET`. Instead they 
+set `GITHUB_ACTIONS` and authenticate using workload identity, so only `AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID` and `AZURE_TENANT_ID` 
+are required in that environment.
+
 A few tests also need the `TEST_BILLING_ID` variable set to a valid Azure Billing ID when running in record mode. 
 In replay mode this variable is never required. Note that the billing ID is redacted from all recording files so that 
 the resulting file can be replayed by anybody, even somebody who does not know the Billing ID the test was recorded with.
